--- /dev/null
+++ b/REVIEW41.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# GharTV Review41 — connection and diagnostics
+
+Owner Review40 installed correctly; this update repairs error isolation and collection visibility without trusting invalid certificates. Every SSL callback still cancels. Only positively observed subresources avoid poisoning the whole document. Unknown or main-document failures remain blocked. The app now shows certificate reason, failed origin (no path/query), TV time and WebView version in Connection. Registered-address choices require explicit navigation with standard TLS; no new domain is trusted and no cookies are copied. No guarantee is made that an external certificate problem can be repaired inside the APK.
+
+Discover now emits consent-gated feature/failure events without titles, search text or provider URLs. Diagnostics adds a manual delivery check (labelled as such, not an install or a view) with actual collector acknowledgement and queued/disabled/error states. Redirects cannot forward the ingest credential; unexpected collector destinations are rejected; incomplete acknowledgement retains the queue. Existing user consent is preserved. Admin access remains in Operon Analytics.
+
+The separate existing Operon Analytics GharTV adapter reads the wrong timestamp field names. The collector exports client_ts/received_at; the old report ignored both and silently discarded received rows. That needs the targeted existing-Analytics source correction; an Android update alone cannot replace a running Python report. Do not call zero displayed events evidence of zero collected data. No actual authenticated owner collector read or owner-TV connection probe was performed in this cloud build.
+
+Tests retain the 70 earlier Android cases (including advancing owned-video clocks) and add 18 TLS scope/queue/delivery/consent regression cases. TLS callback tests invoke the same production handler with a counting cancel action, not a forged trusted certificate; transport tests run real serialization/queue logic with local interceptors, not production uploads. Fixed-host cloud probes test normal TLS only and are not proof of the owner's network or playback. No household41 update is authorized. Published38, original key/data/Nova/web remain unchanged. QR phone remote and Tor remain deferred.
